QtPi firmware artifacts
=======================

The backward-compatible machine-readable release catalog is `manifest.json`
(schema v1). Existing Desktop Suite builds use its single `downloadUrl` per
version. New tooling should use `manifest-v2.json`, which represents releases
as image arrays and links to immutable release descriptors.

ESP32 Firmata releases are stored under:

    veda-esp32/firmata-dual/v<version>/qtpi-esp32-firmata-v<version>.bin

QtPi MicroPython releases are stored under:

    veda-esp32/micropython/v<version>/qtpi-esp32-micropython-v<version>.bin

QtPi MicroPython product versions are independent of the bundled upstream
MicroPython runtime version. Current QtPi images merge the bootloader,
partition table, application, and populated LittleFS partition into one binary
that is flashed at offset `0x0000`.

Each current ESP32 version directory contains `release.json` and
`SHA256SUMS`. Each flavor also has a small `latest.json` pointer. The
`latest/` binary directory remains as a compatibility mirror; versioned
directories are the canonical, immutable publication locations.

JSON schemas live under `schema/`. Validate the full local catalog with:

    python3 tools/firmware/validate_catalog.py
